 "Cells" -> {<|"Data" -> ".md\n# 1 Minute of Verlet Integration: \
Supplementary\nI've made a video recently on one of my favourite methods for \
solving Newton's equations. It is available on YouTube Shorts \|01f3a5\n\nIt \
wasn't clear to me if this is worth a full article or just a short comment. \
Let me start with a supplementary material for the video first, and then we \
shall see...\n\n<details>\n<summary>Actual Video</summary>\n\n<iframe \
width=\"315\" \
height=\"560\"\nsrc=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/6eLUQDEBBHI\"\ntitle=\"Yo\
uTube video player\"\nframeborder=\"0\"\nallow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; \
clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; \
web-share\"\nallowfullscreen=\"true\"></iframe>\n\n</details>", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "c9eefaba-958c-4e1d-be66-6ddea4d0b477", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "# 1 Minute of Verlet Integration: Supplementary\nI've made a \
video recently on one of my favourite methods for solving Newton's equations. \
It is available on YouTube Shorts \|01f3a5\n\nIt wasn't clear to me if this \
is worth a full article or just a short comment. Let me start with a \
supplementary material for the video first, and then we shall \
see...\n\n<details ><summary >Actual Video</summary><iframe width=\"315\" \
height=\"560\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/6eLUQDEBBHI\" \
title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; \
autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; \
web-share\" allowfullscreen=\"true\"></iframe></details>", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "7a6801bf-7be5-469a-a598-7bbe72aba151", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n\n>\n> I've already published a [blog \
post](https://wljs.io/blog/2025/05/01/rim) on the Verlet method, briefly \
mentioning the ideas behind it.\n\n## Basics\nAll credit goes to these \
people:\n\n<div class=\"flex flex-row gap-x-4 mt-2\">\n  \n<figure>\n  \
\n\n<img src=\"/attachments/image-08b.png\" height=\"300\" \
width=\"180\"/>\n\n  <caption>Loup Verlet</caption>\n</figure>\n\n<figure>\n  \
\n\n<img src=\"/attachments/image-08f.png\" height=\"300\" \
width=\"180\"/>\n\n\n  <caption>Carl \
St\[OSlash]rmer</caption>\n</figure>\n\n</div>\n\nAs shown in the video, a \
simple idea leads us to the following numerical solution of both kinematic \
and dynamic problems:\n\n$$\nx_{n+1} = 2 x_{n} - x_{n-1} + \\delta^{2} \
f_{n}/m\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ represents the number of iterations. \n\n### \
Implementation\nThe aforementioned equation translates nicely into computer \
code. Here, for demonstration purposes, I am going to use our beloved \
sandbox, the WLJS Notebook:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "db5a50e7-02f2-4f21-8718-2b91efa04f9d", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ">\n> I've already published a [blog \
post](https://wljs.io/blog/2025/05/01/rim) on the Verlet method, briefly \
mentioning the ideas behind it.\n\n## Basics\nAll credit goes to these \
people:\n\n<div class=\"flex flex-row gap-x-4 mt-2\"><figure ><img \
src=\"/attachments/image-08b.png\" height=\"300\" width=\"180\"/><caption \
>Loup Verlet</caption></figure><figure ><img \
src=\"/attachments/image-08f.png\" height=\"300\" width=\"180\"/><caption \
>Carl St\[OSlash]rmer</caption></figure></div>\n\nAs shown in the video, a \
simple idea leads us to the following numerical solution of both kinematic \
and dynamic problems:\n\n$$\nx_{n+1} = 2 x_{n} - x_{n-1} + \\delta^{2} \
f_{n}/m\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ represents the number of iterations. \n\n### \
Implementation\nThe aforementioned equation translates nicely into computer \
code. Here, for demonstration purposes, I am going to use our beloved \
sandbox, the WLJS Notebook:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "07d6fd13-6477-4ee8-bc98-fc5484694098", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "With[{handler = Unique[], ball = Unique[\"ball\"]},\n  ball = \
Table[{0,0}, {3}];\n  \n  handler = Function[Null,\n    ball[[3]] = \
ball[[2]];\n    ball[[2]] = ball[[1]];\n    \n    ball[[1]] = 2 ball[[2]] - \
ball[[3]] + {0,-1} 0.01;\n    If[ball[[1, 2]] < -1.0, ball[[{1,2}]] = \
ball[[{2,1}]]]; \n    \n    ball = ball;\n  ];\n\n  Graphics[{\n    {Gray, \
Line[{{-1,0}, {1,0}}]},\n    Point[ball[[1]]//Offload],\n    \
EventHandler[AnimationFrameListener[ball//Offload], handler]\n  }, \
PlotRange->{{-1,1}, {-1,1}}, \"Controls\"->False]\n]", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "37fda284-2315-4bf3-9664-dcdac678945a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(Graphics[{{GrayLevel[0.5], Line[{{-1, 0}, {1, 0}}]}, \
Point[Offload[ball42[[1]]]], AnimationFrameListener[Offload[ball42], \
\"Event\" -> \"a441b26f-c521-4c2b-ba84-773c88e4c1d6\"]}, PlotRange -> {{-1, \
1}, {-1, 1}}, \"Controls\" -> \
False])(*,*)(*\"1:eJyNUU1PwzAM7fja9ge4I3HtoV229YYQYnCoRNX9Aid1WCQvQUmYxL/ln0C\
SIpVuHPDhyX7Oe7acG25aOcmyzF0EeDbUyfNYzQI8WXjbKeF6JvZr5bw8G1VJO+9ff9R4QLJZis+7\
wbdWGo90o0p9hVBRdcRHh55PXpcBGqP0z9hpgBcpyUA36Bqw3l2FhAMRK5NF370OcK/VHrwyemNhj\
3EGarQndr8MBuf2nXAbV3g8oPbb25ABYwUvVzIXy7LImSh5zqFi+Xq9EFWFTBTdamyQbtWQ8S3o13\
8cZXJ6lD/4tFr8swejvTXk0qk2QA6/AYJLbLE=\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "812bb79f-068b-4d19-be2c-28a922ccee82", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nAll positions of a single bouncing ball are stored in \
the `ball` symbol. The resulting equations for this case are as \
follows:\n\n$$\n\\\\begin{align*}\n&ball_{n-1} &=& ~ ball_{n} \
\\\\\\\\\n&ball_{n} &=& ~ball_{n+1} \\\\\\\\\n&ball_{n+1} &=& ~2 ball_{n} - \
ball_{n-1} + \\\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\\\\\ -1 \\\\end{bmatrix} \
\\\\alpha^2\n\\\\end{align*}\n$$\n\n\nwhere the last term $\\alpha$ \
represents the gravitational force.\n\n__Additionally__, we consider the \
boundary conditions: if a ball crosses the ground, we exchange $ball_{n}$ and \
$ball_{n+1}$, which implicitly flips the \
velocity\n\n!![{\"id\":\"aaojXbsu5k65SYzW3y47I\",\"type\":\"line\",\"x\":88.8\
