    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "All positions of a single bouncing ball are stored in the \
`ball` symbol. The resulting equations for this case are as \
follows:\n\n$$\n\\\\begin{align*}\n&ball_{n-1} &=& ~ ball_{n} \
\\\\\\\\\n&ball_{n} &=& ~ball_{n+1} \\\\\\\\\n&ball_{n+1} &=& ~2 ball_{n} - \
ball_{n-1} + \\\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\\\\\ -1 \\\\end{bmatrix} \
\\\\alpha^2\n\\\\end{align*}\n$$\n\n\nwhere the last term $\\alpha$ \
represents the gravitational force.\n\n__Additionally__, we consider the \
boundary conditions: if a ball crosses the ground, we exchange $ball_{n}$ and \
$ball_{n+1}$, which implicitly flips the velocity\n\n\n<div \
class=\"text-center w-full\"><svg version=\"1.1\" \
xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 716.791412115097 \
256.44140625\">\n  <!-- svg-source:excalidraw -->\n  \n  <defs>\n    <style \
class=\"style-fonts\">\n      @font-face {\n        font-family: \
\"Virgil\";\n        src: \
url(\"https://unpkg.com/@excalidraw/excalidraw@undefined/dist/excalidraw-asse\
ts/Virgil.woff2\");\n      }\n      @font-face {\n        font-family: \
\"Cascadia\";\n        src: \
