    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "e688b900-55ab-4bd4-9499-c9a9e6d6358c", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n### Loses\nTo consider inelastic case we should simply \
reduce the reflected momentum (or velocity in our case).", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "4ec345a8-3f69-411c-ac3b-02ef09320a08", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "### Loses\nTo consider inelastic case we should simply reduce \
the reflected momentum (or velocity in our case).", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "93c81391-625f-4cb5-a55e-e533ceb5fabe", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "With[{handler = Unique[], ball = Unique[\"ball\"]},\n  ball = \
Table[{0,0}, {3}];\n  \n  handler = Function[Null,\n    ball[[3]] = \
ball[[2]];\n    ball[[2]] = ball[[1]];\n    \n    ball[[1]] = 2 ball[[2]] - \
ball[[3]] + {0,-1} 0.01;\n    If[ball[[1, 2]] < -1.0, \n      With[{vel = \
ball[[1]]-ball[[2]]},\n        ball[[2]] = ball[[1]];\n        ball[[1]] = \
ball[[1]] - 0.95 vel;\n      ];\n    ];\n    \n    ball = ball;\n  ];\n\n  \
Graphics[{\n    {Gray, Line[{{-1,0}, {1,0}}]},\n    \
Point[ball[[1]]//Offload],\n    \
EventHandler[AnimationFrameListener[ball//Offload], handler]\n  }, \
PlotRange->{{-1,1}, {-1,1}}, \"Controls\"->False]\n]", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "6714bd32-aba1-409a-8fe9-cabf1db55377", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> " ", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "18a4f0e5-f80c-4037-990b-513a99af200a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## General Boundary Conditions\nI guess for the simplest \
case, our trick with flipping the velocity works well. However, for a surface \
at an angle, it might not work well, since we need to mirror the velocity \
along the plane defined by some kind of __normal vector__.\n\nIt is a nice \
exercise you can try at \
