   <|"Data" -> ".md\n### Momentum Transfer\nA rim itself (or a circle, if you \
wish) also has velocity and momentum. However, for now, it cannot be \
transferred to our ball.\n\nHow can we do that without violating the \
physics?\n\n> Whenever you have troubles, move to some other __Frame of \
Reference__\n\nBy moving our calculations to the frame of reference of our \
rim, we remove this puzzle completely. Then we solve our boundary problem \
there, and afterward move back to the original static frame of \
reference:\n\n!![{\"type\":\"ellipse\",\"version\":50,\"versionNonce\":209802\
