    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Constraint Algorithm\n\nWhenever you try to model a \
system with multiple hard or soft bonds connecting different nodes, it \
quickly becomes a pain. This is one of those cases where solving the problem \
using only positions\[LongDash]without momentum and forces-becomes a game \
changer.\n\nAs mentioned in [my previous \
post](https://wljs.io/blog/2025/05/01/rim):\n\n> By directly adjusting the \
positions of two points connected by a bond to maintain the bond length, we \
effectively account for all forces in a single step.  \n> The stiffness of \
the bond is not directly part of the differential equation\[LongDash]it's \
introduced through how you enforce the constraint: either strictly (hard) or \
partially \
(soft).\n\n!![{\"type\":\"ellipse\",\"version\":122,\"versionNonce\":72860706\
