215.94, -1.4 163.22, 0 32 M0 270.14 C1.48 179.79, 1.2 90.52, 0 32 M0 32 C1 \
8.95, 10.1 0.48, 32 0 M0 32 C1.21 8.48, 11.56 2.2, 32 0\" \
stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"1\" \
fill=\"none\"></path></g></svg></div>\n\nFirstly, we perform a normal Verlet \
update and then apply constraints. Since each bond affects both vertices, the \
\"information\" (momentum, tension, etc.) travels through all nodes of the \
system. This allows, for instance, if our *mesh* hits the ground with one of \
its vertices, the whole body will stop and bounce back.\n\nIn addition, I \
will give an example similar to what you have seen in the video:\n\n### Image \
to Mesh\n*Transformation of the b/w image to a mesh of interconnected \
vertices*\n\n:::tip\nGo to the header section to download this notebook\n:::"\
, "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> "4fa6d059-9619-41b1-99c4-23326a557400", 
    "Invisible" -> False, "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> 
     "(dude = NotebookStore[\"cob-105\"] // NotebookRead)//Colorize ", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "ae5fbff6-79e5-4c4a-968a-899cc4968064", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"f689ba6c-806f-4606-8ca2-ebf725f42548\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKp5lZW\
CYlmiXrWhiYpemamBmY6VokJxrppialmRuZppkYmZpYAACGoRWG\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "b4831f2a-81c8-4cce-8c08-1324c22f5f64", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nNow transform it into bonds:", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "4735bf86-f43c-4d85-ad31-10ba06136e1a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Now transform it into bonds:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "2b258e42-02d0-4877-ba9a-666d1cf811b8", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "SetAttributes[UndirectedEdge, Orderless];\n\ngetMesh[img_] := \
With[{mesh = TriangulateMesh[ImageMesh[img], \
MaxCellMeasure->{\"Area\"->45}]}, Module[{\n  vertices = \
MeshCoordinates[mesh],\n  edges = (Cases[mesh//MeshCells, _Polygon, 2] /. {\n \
 Polygon[{a_, b_, c_}] :> Sequence[UndirectedEdge[a,b], UndirectedEdge[b,c], \
UndirectedEdge[a,c]]\n} // DeleteDuplicates) /. {UndirectedEdge -> \
List}\n},\n  {vertices, edges}\n] ]", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "36c40af8-e258-4fff-9ac9-5bc905b12450", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nAnd apply to our `dude`", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "f04624c0-b387-49cf-9488-38d12fdd8a38", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "And apply to our `dude`", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "65e25458-49d6-4e78-9191-b73510e7729c", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "NotebookWrite[NotebookStore[\"dudeMesh\"], dude // \
getMesh];\ndude // getMesh;\nGraphics[GraphicsComplex[%[[1]], {Line /@ \
%[[2]]}]]", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "a04be72e-1e09-4f3f-a90e-5b9114fd985a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"3bb3903f-7fe8-4344-8870-49d66474905c\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKGyclG\
VsaGKfpmqelWuiaGJuY6FpYmBvomlimmJmZmJtYGpgmAwB6kxTM\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "6f40b4f6-b9c5-4e9b-9586-d215dbcf06c4", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n### Rendering\nThere is an issue with the traditional \
approach to animating using `Graphics` when dealing with numerous line \
segments. Typically, you might use `GraphicsComplex`, but as of now, it does \
not support updates. This may change in the future. This means that if the \
data changes, it won't be reflected. Working with individual `Line` \
primitives seems like a good plan (as was done in the previous post), but for \
the sake of performance, we shall use a 2D raster canvas here:", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "0d558699-ad32-48f0-b57c-6417da83e32f", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "### Rendering\nThere is an issue with the traditional \
approach to animating using `Graphics` when dealing with numerous line \
segments. Typically, you might use `GraphicsComplex`, but as of now, it does \
not support updates. This may change in the future. This means that if the \
data changes, it won't be reflected. Working with individual `Line` \
primitives seems like a good plan (as was done in the previous post), but for \
the sake of performance, we shall use a 2D raster canvas here:", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "3ba86bfa-a6cb-4d18-bb8b-047884ae409f", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Needs[\"Canvas2D`\"->\"ctx`\"] // Quiet;", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "da96d952-d724-43ba-8943-da3e58a2e38e", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"InitGroup" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
