8,\"version\":125,\"versionNonce\":1788242524,\"isDeleted\":false,\"boundElem\
ents\":null,\"updated\":1753620741774,\"link\":null,\"locked\":false}]\n\nUnf\
ortunately, this also means that the complexity of our algorithm scales as \
$N^2$, where $N$ is the number of our particles, leading to performance \
issues. There are many ways to deal with this, but the easiest one would be \
to compile our little program.\n\nFortunately, there is a built-in expression \
`Compile` that allows us to directly translate Wolfram Language code to C or \
internal bytecode. Of course, it comes with restrictions on statically typed \
data structures and other limitations:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
