dominant-baseline=\"text-before-edge\">d/2</text></g><g \
stroke-linecap=\"round\" transform=\"translate(10 10) rotate(0 365.734375 \
117.861328125)\"><path d=\"M32 0 C296.81 0.08, 560.97 1.47, 699.47 0 M32 0 \
C238.86 1.82, 445.65 1.91, 699.47 0 M699.47 0 C721.3 -0.51, 731.3 12.63, \
731.47 32 M699.47 0 C719.52 -1.96, 733.32 9.92, 731.47 32 M731.47 32 C731.87 \
81.59, 732.68 132.71, 731.47 203.72 M731.47 32 C732.5 97.48, 732.41 162.17, \
731.47 203.72 M731.47 203.72 C729.77 224.78, 722.24 235.73, 699.47 235.72 \
M731.47 203.72 C730.15 227.01, 722.48 237.24, 699.47 235.72 M699.47 235.72 \
C471.8 235.44, 244.58 235.31, 32 235.72 M699.47 235.72 C479.1 237.47, 257.77 \
236.92, 32 235.72 M32 235.72 C11.43 235.7, -0.8 225.17, 0 203.72 M32 235.72 \
C11.18 233.53, -1.55 224.89, 0 203.72 M0 203.72 C-1.37 139.67, 0.56 78.05, 0 \
32 M0 203.72 C-1.09 153.48, -1.09 103.97, 0 32 M0 32 C1.05 8.77, 12.59 0.11, \
32 0 M0 32 C-1.26 8.97, 12.5 0.51, 32 0\" stroke=\"transparent\" \
stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"></path></g></svg></div>\n\n\nUnfortunately, \
this also means that the complexity of our algorithm scales as $N^2$, where \
$N$ is the number of our particles, leading to performance issues. There are \
many ways to deal with this, but the easiest one would be to compile our \
little program.\n\nFortunately, there is a built-in expression `Compile` that \
allows us to directly translate Wolfram Language code to C or internal \
bytecode. Of course, it comes with restrictions on statically typed data \
structures and other limitations:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "508ebc06-3474-42ea-8e61-d4cb0bbbe3cf", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "compiled = Compile[{\n  {p, _Real, 3}, {c, _Real, 2}, \
{target, _Real, 1}\n}, Module[{b = p, \\[Delta]t = 0.005, circ = c},\n    \
Do[\n      circ[[1]] = circ[[1]] + \\[Delta]t (target - circ[[1]]);\n      \n \
     b[[{1,2}]] = MapThread[If[Norm[#1-circ[[2]]] > 1.0, Module[{\n        u \
= {#1, #2},\n        vel = (circ[[1]] - circ[[2]])\n      },\n\n        \n    \
    u[[1]] = u[[1]] - vel;\n        \n        \n        With[{n = \
-Normalize[u[[1]]-circ[[2]]], delta = u[[1]]-u[[2]]},\n          u[[2]] = \
u[[1]];\n          u[[1]] = u[[1]] -  0.9 n (n.delta);\n        ];\n\n        \
u[[1]] = u[[1]] + vel;\n\n        If[Norm[u[[1]]-circ[[2]]] > 1.0, (*clamp to \
the region *)\n          u[[1]] += (1.0 - Norm[u[[1]]-circ[[2]]]) \
Normalize[u[[1]]-circ[[2]]];\n        ];\n\n        u\n      ], {#1, #2}]&, \
{b[[1]], b[[2]]}] // Transpose;\n\n      b[[3]] = b[[2]];\n      b[[2]] = \
b[[1]];\n      b[[1]] = 2 b[[2]] - b[[3]] + Table[{0,-1}, {Length[b[[1]]]}] \
(*SpB[*)Power[\\[Delta]t(*|*),(*|*)2](*]SpB*);\n\n\n    (* Particle-particle \
collisions *)\n    Do[\n      Do[\n        If[i < j,\n          Module[{pi = \
b[[1, i]], pj = b[[1, j]], d, dist, n, overlap},\n            d = pj - pi;\n  \
          dist = Norm[d];\n            If[dist < 0.05,\n              n = \
Normalize[d];\n              overlap = 0.05 - dist;\n              b[[1, i]] \
-= 0.5 overlap n;\n              b[[1, j]] += 0.5 overlap n;\n            \
];\n          ]\n        ],\n        {j, Length[b[[1]]]}\n      ],\n      {i, \
Length[b[[1]]]}\n    ];   \n\n\n      circ[[2]] = circ[[1]];\n    , \
{10}];\n\n    b[[-1, 1]] = circ[[1]];\n    b[[-1, 2]] = circ[[2]];\n\n    b\n \
 ], CompilationOptions -> {\"InlineExternalDefinitions\" -> True}, \n    \
\"CompilationTarget\" -> \"C\",\"RuntimeOptions\" -> \"Speed\"];", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "81a80b07-53bd-4481-976d-b911ecfa8b9b", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"InitGroup" -> True, "Fade" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nPlease, don't be confised by the design of inputs and \
outputs of this compiled function. In Wolfram Language `Compile`ed \
expressions cannot return nested structures, therfore we have to trick and \
sort of serialize the data into a numerical tensor and then deserialize back. \
In this case it is done using `Part`.", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "b8620201-2826-46b6-8483-0f84aba58f6a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Please, don't be confised by the design of the input and \
output of this compiled function. In Wolfram Language `Compile`ed expressions \
cannot return nested structures, therfore we have to trick and sort of \
serialize the data into a numerical tensor and then deserialize back. In this \
case it is done using `Part`.", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "9fceb167-c0ef-4d99-afc6-0d3fab2894b7", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nThe rest is on us, i.e. to plug our function back into \
the main loop:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "a79ca812-ce33-4ebf-81cc-a26a0828f630", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> 
     "The rest is on us, i.e. to plug our function back into the main loop:", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "ba6efcb9-e4e8-417d-8214-e5b370598bc4", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "With[{\n  p = Unique[\"ppp\"],\n  toDraw = Unique[\"ppp\"],\n \
 circ = Unique[\"ppp\"],\n  target = Unique[\"ppp\"],\n  frame = \
CreateUUID[]\n},\n  p = Table[Exp[-i/80.0]{Sin[i], Cos[i]}, {3}, {i, 100}];\n \
 toDraw = p[[1]];\n  circ = {{0,0}, {0,0}};\n  target = {0,0};\n\n  \
EventHandler[frame, Function[Null,\n      With[{\n        c = \
compiled[Join[p, {p[[3]]}], circ, target]\n      },\n        circ = c[[4, \
{1,2}]];\n        p = c[[1;;3]];\n        toDraw = p[[1]];\n      ]\n  \
]];\n\n  {\n    Graphics[{\n      PointSize[0.03],\n      Circle[circ[[1]] // \
Offload, 1.0], \n      Pink, Point[toDraw // Offload],\n      \
AnimationFrameListener[p//Offload, \"Event\"->frame]\n    }, \n      \
PlotRange->{1.4{-1,1}, 1.4{-1,1}}, \n      AspectRatio->1, ImageSize->Medium, \
\n      TransitionType->None\n    ],\n\n    EventHandler[InputJoystick[], \
Function[xy, target = xy;]]\n  } // Row\n]", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "5734ddb3-94e3-4137-892e-d3523b556f6e", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Fade" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> " ", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "113eaab1-55f7-4646-b2e9-d7d741a809a2", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "b1000fb1-c9cc-423c-925a-13fafc2266f2"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nAs you can see, one can go quite far using this toolbox. \
 \nHope you\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve learned something fun today! \|01faf6\n\nFeel \
free to share thoughts or ask questions in the comments.", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "40af6f2b-3f0e-43d0-9932-f1a31a817e90", "Invisible" -> False, 
